  "summary": {
    "en": {
      "caveats": "The paper is a theoretical perspective and does not present empirical data, quantitative modeling, or a concrete implementation of the proposed framework.",
      "what": "This perspective introduces the Ecoadaptive Intelligence Theory, a conceptual framework that reframes urban systems as socio-ecological-computational assemblages. The theory shifts the focus of urban intelligence from prediction, optimisation, and control toward co-learning and adaptive responses driven by spatial form and environmental feedback.",
      "why": "It challenges the dominant smart city paradigm by showing that traditional optimization models are insufficient for the deep uncertainty of climate change, offering a new theoretical pathway to integrate ecological feedback directly into urban computational systems."
